// Distributed-rows schedule: 4 compute workers row-band partition the
// OUTPUT's row axis. Output is declared `i32[W][H]` with W=16 (rows)
// and H=8 (cols), so the output-row index is the variable `j` (which
// in the algorithm's for-nest sits as the INNER loop). Each worker
// owns 4 contiguous output rows (W=16 / 4 = 4 exact-divisible).
//
// Landing TASK-0341.01 AC#2 follow-out, cycle 215. The schedule
// exercises a STRUCTURAL FIRST for the cross-backend matrix: a
// partition where the partition iv hits one data's LEADING dim and
// another data's TRAILING dim under axis-swap permutation.
//
// Partition axis choice (partition=workers on the inner j-loop, NOT
// partition=rows)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// `partition=rows` (TASK-0258, partition_rows.rs:1-30) is the
// outer-of-2D Repeat-of-Repeat directive — it applies to the OUTER
// loop of a 2D nest, not the inner. The transpose's output-row axis
// is `j` (the W=16-bound index), which sits at the INNER loop
// position in the algorithm's for-nest. `partition=workers`
// (TASK-0212, partition_workers.rs:1-105) is the more flexible
// directive: `find_loop` does a recursive descent and can target
// the inner j-loop directly.
//
// What this exercises in the compiler
// -----------------------------------
// - `partition=workers` on an inner loop (no shipped schedule had
//   done this before — every prior `partition=workers` cell hits
//   the outer-most loop). Sanity-check that `find_loop`'s
//   recursive descent correctly targets the inner Repeat.
//
// - The TASK-0301/TASK-0302 axis-mapping filter
//   (`compute_partition_bounds_with_dim_prefix`, transfer_inject.rs:2418)
//   under axis-swap permutation:
//     * `output[j][i]` — dim 0 = j (partitioned), dim 1 = i (not
//       partitioned). Walk: dim 0 Some(j_band) → push; dim 1 None →
//       hit_hole. Final bounds = [(j, j_band)]: output is j-banded
//       on gather (4 contiguous rows per worker).
//     * `input[i][j]` — dim 0 = i (not partitioned), dim 1 = j
//       (partitioned). Walk: dim 0 None → hit_hole; dim 1 Some(j_band)
//       AFTER hole → return Some(empty). Empty bounds → whole-array
//       broadcast.
//
//   The asymmetric per-data outcome (output j-banded, input
//   whole-array) is the contiguous-prefix invariant biting on the
//   axis-swap shape. It is the CORRECT graceful-degradation path
//   per the cycle-118/121 design: a non-contiguous coverage shape
//   degrades safely to whole-array broadcast rather than emitting
//   silently wrong tile bounds. Structural twin of 07-matmul ×
//   distributed-2d (cycle 121, TASK-0302), where `b[k][j]` ×
//   partition=blocks2d(i,j) hits the same sparse-coverage →
//   Some(empty) → broadcast shape. What is structurally NEW in
//   15-transpose vs 07-matmul/distributed-2d is the inner-loop
//   partition target (`loop j : partition=workers` reaches the
//   inner j-loop via partition_workers::find_loop's recursive
//   descent — every prior `partition=workers` cell targeted the
//   outermost loop of the for-nest).
//
// Why bit-identical is achievable
// -------------------------------
// The xpose kernel is pure identity. Each output element
// output[j][i] = input[i][j] depends only on a single input element;
// no reduction, no halo, no cross-iteration carry. Each worker
// computes a disjoint slice of output[][] (its j-band rows × full
// i cols = 32 of 128 elements). The host gathers all 4 slices into
// the final output buffer.
//
// Why sync transfers
// ------------------
// Sync-only schedule lowers on every tier-1 backend
// (pthreads-sync, mp-tcp-bufsync, pthreads-async, mp-tcp-event,
// openmp-rs, mp-tcp-poll, mp-uds-event) without capability gaps.
// Cross-backend promotion to all 7 tier-1 backends landed cycle
// 216 (TASK-0341.01.01.01); cell-level [[required]] state in
// nuc-nucleus/e2e-matrix.toml. Initial pthreads-sync landing was
// cycle 215 (TASK-0341.01.01).

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host, w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    place load_input  on host;
    place save_output on host;
    place xpose       on { w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // Row-band partition the inner j axis (output's leading "row"
    // axis under the [W][H] layout). W=16 / 4 workers → 4 j-values
    // each, exact-divisible.
    loop j : partition=workers;

    // input is whole-array broadcast (axis-swap → trailing-dim
    // coverage → contiguous-prefix filter returns empty bounds).
    // output is j-banded on gather (leading-dim coverage → bounds
    // = [(j, j_band)]).
    transfer input  : sync;
    transfer output : sync;
}
